				</ukm:Metadata><Secondary><Body DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/nisi/1995/2994/body" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/nisi/1995/2994/body" NumberOfProvisions="118" RestrictStartDate="2020-12-31"><Part DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/nisi/1995/2994/part/II" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/nisi/1995/2994/part/II" NumberOfProvisions="57" id="part-II" RestrictStartDate="2020-12-31"><Number>PART II</Number><Title>Principal Road Safety Provisions</Title><Pblock DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/nisi/1995/2994/part/II/crossheading/driving-offences" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/nisi/1995/2994/part/II/crossheading/driving-offences" NumberOfProvisions="7" RestrictExtent="N.I." RestrictStartDate="2008-07-16" id="part-II-crossheading-driving-offences"><Title>Driving Offences</Title><P1group RestrictStartDate="2006-01-01"><Title>Careless, and inconsiderate, driving</Title><P1 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/nisi/1995/2994/article/12" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/nisi/1995/2994/article/12" id="article-12"><Pnumber>12</Pnumber><P1para><Text>If a person drives a mechanically propelled vehicle on a road or other public place without due care and attention, or without reasonable consideration for other persons using the road or place, he is guilty of an offence.</Text></P1para></P1></P1group></Pblock></Part></Body></Secondary></Legislation>